.TH MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-SERVER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-notify-server \- Mu2e DAQ notification server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-notify-server
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-db\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-dynamic\-base\-url\fR | \fB\-\-no\-dynamic\-base\-url\fR]
[\fB\-\-trusted\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR]...
[\fB\-\-tls\fR | \fB\-\-no\-tls\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-adhoc\fR]
[\fB\-\-api\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]... [\fB\-\-zmq\fR | \fB\-\-no\-zmq\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-discovery\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives error and warning events from Mu2e DAQ applications, stores them,
matches them against filter rules held in the database, and delivers them to
registered iPhones (Apple Push Notification service), Slack and Discord
incoming webhooks, and a live Server\-Sent Events web dashboard.
.PP
Two ingest paths share one normalizer
.RB ( normalize_event ()
in
.IR src/mu2edaq_notify/events.py ):
the HTTP API
.RB ( "POST /api/events" ,
bearer\-token authenticated), and an optional ZeroMQ compatibility listener
(PULL bound at
.BR zmq.bind ,
default
.BR tcp://0.0.0.0:8096 ,
plus SUB sockets connected to each
.B zmq.connect
endpoint). Both paths read only the notify event keys
.RB ( source ,
.BR host ,
.BR severity ,
.BR category ,
.BR title ,
.BR message ,
.BR timestamp ,
.BR meta ).
A JSON payload in the
.B mu2edaq\-dashboard
schema
.RB ( error_level ,
.BR subsystem ,
.BR event_category )
is accepted on the ZeroMQ listener but none of those keys is read, so every
such message arrives with severity
.B zmq.default_severity
(\fBwarning\fR), source
.BR zmq ,
and no category, whatever its level. Under the shipped
.B errors\-to\-phones
rule
.RB ( "min_severity: error" )
a dashboard
.B error
therefore pages nobody. See
.I docs/INTERFACES.md
section 3.
.PP
Delivery runs on one daemon thread that drains an unbounded queue and calls
each matched destination in turn with a 10 s HTTP timeout and no retry; every
attempt is recorded in the
.B deliveries
table as
.BR sent ,
.BR logged ,
.B failed
or
.BR suppressed .
.PP
The server announces itself with the mu2edaq\-discovery protocol
.RB ( app=notify )
when the
.B mu2edaq_discovery
package is importable and
.B discovery.enabled
is true. The ANNOUNCE carries this host's own address
.RB ( discovery.host / port / scheme ,
empty by default meaning this machine's FQDN, the server port, and
http or https to match TLS) and, in
.BR meta.fallback_url ,
the public reverse\-proxy URL publishers should try only when the local
address is unreachable.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option overrides the matching configuration key. A list\-valued option
.RB ( \-\-api\-token ,
.BR \-\-trusted\-host )
.B replaces
the list from the configuration file; tokens read from
.B auth.api_tokens_file
are then appended to it.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
YAML configuration file. Default:
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CONFIG .
There is no built\-in default path: with neither set, the server runs on
built\-in defaults only. A path that does not exist is
.B silently ignored
and the built\-in defaults are used, which include no publisher tokens.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDR"
Bind address
.RB ( server.host ,
default 0.0.0.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Bind port
.RB ( server.port ,
default 8095).
.TP
.BI \-\-db\-url " URL"
SQLAlchemy database URL
.RB ( database.url ,
default
.BR sqlite:///data/notify.db ,
relative to the working directory). Use
.B postgresql+psycopg2://
for Postgres; the
.B postgres
extra provides the driver. The URL is written to the startup log line
verbatim, password included.
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-url " URL"
Fallback public base URL for enrollment QR codes and auto\-configuration
payloads
.RB ( server.base_url ).
With dynamic resolution on it is used only when the request host is malformed
or, with an allowlist set, not on it.
.TP
.BR \-\-dynamic\-base\-url ", " \-\-no\-dynamic\-base\-url
Derive the enrollment URL from each request (leftmost
.BR X\-Forwarded\-Host / X\-Forwarded\-Proto ,
else the request's own
.B Host
and scheme), or always use
.BR \-\-base\-url .
Default on
.RB ( server.dynamic_base_url ).
.TP
.BI \-\-trusted\-host " HOST"
Restrict dynamic resolution to this hostname or
.B *.suffix
pattern; repeatable
.RB ( server.trusted_hosts ).
The request host is always checked against the hostname grammar; with no
allowlist any well\-formed host is accepted.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls ", " \-\-no\-tls
Serve HTTPS from the built\-in server using
.BR server.tls ,
or plain HTTP
.RB ( server.tls.enabled ,
default false). iOS App Transport Security requires HTTPS for enrollment, so
either this or a TLS\-terminating proxy is needed for phones.
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-\-tls\-key\fR \fIFILE\fR
Certificate chain and private key
.RB ( server.tls.cert_file ,
.BR server.tls.key_file ).
Both are required when TLS is on without
.BR \-\-tls\-adhoc ;
the server refuses to start if either is unset or missing.
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-adhoc
HTTPS with a throwaway self\-signed certificate; implies
.BR \-\-tls .
Development only.
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-token " TOKEN"
Publisher bearer token; repeatable
.RB ( auth.api_tokens ).
When no token is configured from any source,
.B POST /api/events
accepts anonymous publishes and the server logs one warning at startup.
Read endpoints
.RB ( "GET /api/events" ,
.BR "GET /api/stream" )
are open to requests that send
.B no
Authorization header whenever
.B auth.oidc.enabled
is false, whether or not tokens are configured.
.TP
.BR \-\-zmq ", " \-\-no\-zmq
Enable or disable the ZeroMQ compatibility listener
.RB ( zmq.enabled ,
default false). Requires
.BR pyzmq ;
without it the listener logs one warning and exits while the HTTP server
keeps running.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-discovery
Do not announce via mu2edaq\-discovery
.RB ( discovery.enabled ).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Flask debug mode, which enables the interactive Werkzeug debugger. Never use
it on an address reachable by anyone else.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/notify-server.yaml
Shipped configuration, used by
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1).
It enables TLS with site\-specific certificate paths and APNs with a specific
key identity; adapt it before use on another host.
.TP
.I config/apns_key.p8
APNs ES256 provider key (path from
.BR apns.key_file ,
relative to the working directory). Not committed. If it cannot be read the
APNs sender drops to log\-only mode for the life of the process; the only
signals are one ERROR log line and deliveries recorded as
.BR logged .
.TP
.I auth.api_tokens
One publisher token per line, lines starting with # ignored (path from
.BR auth.api_tokens_file ).
Not committed. A missing file is silently skipped.
.TP
.I data/notify.db
SQLite database (default
.BR database.url ).
.TP
.IR data/notify-server.log ", " data/notify-server.pid
Log and pid file written by
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each variable overrides one configuration key; values are parsed as YAML, so
.BR true ,
.B 8095
and
.B [a, b]
are typed. A scalar value given for a list\-valued key is
.B appended
to the list (so
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_API_TOKEN=x
adds one token); a YAML list replaces it.
.PP
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CONFIG ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_HOST ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_PORT ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_BASE_URL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DYNAMIC_BASE_URL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TRUSTED_HOSTS ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TLS_ENABLED ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TLS_CERT_FILE ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TLS_KEY_FILE ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TLS_ADHOC ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DB_URL ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_API_TOKEN ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_API_TOKENS_FILE ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_APNS_ENABLED ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ZMQ_ENABLED ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ZMQ_BIND ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DISCOVERY_ENABLED ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DISCOVERY_HOST ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DISCOVERY_PORT ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DISCOVERY_SCHEME ,
.BR MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DISCOVERY_FALLBACK_URL ,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY
(appends one entry to
.BR categories ).
.PP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_WEB_DIR
overrides the directory holding
.I templates/
and
.IR static/ .
.PP
Precedence: command line > environment > configuration file > built\-in
defaults.
.B server.secret_key
and
.B auth.enrollment_secret
are generated randomly per process when empty and are not persisted: a
restart signs out web sessions and invalidates outstanding enrollment codes.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 after a clean shutdown. 1 when startup fails with an uncaught exception,
most often the TLS check
.RB ( "server.tls.enabled requires cert_file/key_file" ,
or
.BR "TLS file does not exist" ),
or a database URL that cannot be opened. 2 on a command\-line usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground with the shipped configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
venv/bin/mu2edaq\-notify\-server \-\-config config/notify\-server.yaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Plain HTTP behind a TLS\-terminating reverse proxy, with a publisher token,
an enrollment\-host allowlist, and the ZeroMQ listener on:
.PP
.RS
.nf
venv/bin/mu2edaq\-notify\-server \-\-config config/notify\-server.yaml \e
    \-\-no\-tls \-\-api\-token "$NOTIFY_TOKEN" \e
    \-\-trusted\-host '*.fnal.gov' \-\-zmq
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check it is up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl \-sk https://localhost:8095/api/health
.fi
.RE
